+      is of requests not yet in the engine's active set, which is as large as its
+      batch. The default scheduler (GUARANTEED_NO_EVICT) never preempts: with the KV
+      cache spoken for it leaves a request in the set and out of the step, and such a
+      request is one of num_requests_running and not one of num_scheduled_requests. The
+      difference does not count them, though. A request that ended in the step before
+      is still in the set and is not scheduled either, and the samples are of just
